      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To implement the dead_letter.py file, I need to select a concrete external provider for messaging. Given the task requirements, I will use Amazon Web Services (AWS) Simple Queue Service (SQS) as the provider. SQS is a managed message queuing service that enables decoupling and scaling of microservices, distributed systems, and serverless applications. It supports dead-letter queues, which are queues that other (source) queues can target for messages that can't be processed successfully.\n\nThe code will include the boto3 library, which is the AWS SDK for Python, to interact with SQS. This will make the provider identifiable in the code. </thinking>\n",
